    {
      "exercise": "217",
      "method": "Let the perpendicular leg lengths be u,v>0 in dm. Require u+v=k and uv=2S. Thus u,v solve t^2-kt+2S=0. For k>0,S>0, existence is equivalent to k^2-8S>=0, or 0<S<=k^2/8. Equal positive legs at equality form a valid right triangle.",
      "a)": "No. k=60,S=500 gives discriminant 3600-4000=-400. Equivalently the largest possible area is 60^2/8=450 dm^2, smaller than 500 dm^2.",
